{
  "modules": [
    {
      "id": "88",
      "def_name": "modular_agent_std::ui::NoteModule",
      "configs": {
        "note": "# Jev (TypeSafe AI System One) showcase\n\nEvery Jev module takes the value to judge on its `state` port (string, object, or array) and asks System One a fixed question about it. The answer is a small JSON object, never free text.\n\n**Setup**: put your key in **Settings → Module → System One → TypeSafe API Key** (or export `TYPESAFE_API_KEY`), start the patch, then press the Unit Input on the left. The same customer message feeds all four rows.\n\n- **Noul** (row 1): a yes/no question. `noul` is the probability that the instructions hold for the input.\n- **Choice** (row 2): pick one label from `criteria` (label → description, or `null`). The Get Value module pulls `choice` out of the answer; wire that into Switch / If for branching.\n- **Score** (row 3): place the input on an ordered scale of 2–10 entries. The Template String module formats `score` and `confidence` into a sentence.\n- **System One** (row 4): several named questions in one request. The output is the whole response (`model`, `answers`, `usage`). Its `err` port is wired to the Display on the right, so a missing key or a rejected request shows up there.\n\nEdit the Text Input to try other messages."
      },
      "config_specs": {
        "note": {
          "value": "",
          "type": "markdown",
          "hide_title": true
        }
      },
      "height": 509,
      "width": 980,
      "x": -1025.0751680811916,
      "y": 247.4789021763048
